    dc:description "Geodesicity has an explicit geometric test. Existing archives may contain spicule ultrastructure, but likely lack simultaneous high-resolution cell-surface reconstructions needed to resolve the mechanism.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Reconstruct the contemporaneous cell surface and spicule centerline in 3D, then test whether the centerline has near-zero geodesic curvature and fits the shortest surface path better than unconstrained growth models. Multiple developmental stages would test the proposed confinement mechanism.";
